# the pinned grammar versions in Cargo.toml are the contract; the
# lockfile is a build by-product here, not a distributed artifact
Cargo.lock
target/
# the fourteen samples are fixtures for the probe, not files of this
# repository. They stay tracked (`git add -f`); this pattern is what
# keeps them out of ce's two walks, which read .gitignore PATTERNS and
# never the index — so they enter neither the scan nor the advisory's
# mention universe (the universe formula counts them under
# pattern-ignored, the zod corpus precedent; a .ceignore is refused).
snippets/
